{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And now our soul is dried up.</b> They said: the manna is destined to be absorbed within our bellies to kill us — that is, is there any human being who does not excrete what he eats? They said to Rabbi Shimon: and how do you fulfill 'and it shall be a peg for you upon your ear' (i.e., how do you explain the verse about digestion)? He said to them: what merchants of the nations of the world bring in to them — from that they excrete; but the manna is never excreted from them, as it is written: 'לחם אבירים אכל איש.' Another interpretation: after they spoiled, they did excrete."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:24.745367779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}